BEGIN_DESC
Titan, northern summer (June 2017), local morning: the Sun ~25 deg up in the east. Southern Kraken Mare, the head of a drowned river valley (ria) on the eastern shore of a peninsula, ~59.33 N 40.49 E (site of the Titan surface work: Orbitersdk/samples/TitanSite).
A river mouth on the low cobble shore (alluvial fan, Huygens-site look). The heavy suit "Pantsir" (Niza Krit) ~15 m from the liquid, facing the sea to the east; the EMPU with its headlights on 75 m inland, and Kaira Rean in the Suit_T10 with the flight module next to it. The MPU 5 m ahead of the EMPU (east), facing the same way - rear to the EMPU's front, to tow it (couple at 2..4 m between the pins: back it up ~1 m). Sea level -617 m.
Light: the haze (Huygens DISR: vertical extinction 3-5.5, blue absorbed by tholins) leaves ~0.1% of Earth's daylight, diffuse and orange, almost no shadows; visibility of kilometres near the ground. Saturn is ~23 deg up in the SW but hidden by the haze.
Air: 1.5 bar N2 at 94 K - calm, dense, cold. The liquid is methane/ethane: dark, mirror-flat, seen by the reflected orange sky.
Visual atmosphere: Config/GC/Titan.atm.cfg (AtmoFX fork of D3D9Client, AtmoFX_MieAbs); the physical atmosphere (Config/Titan.cfg) is unchanged.
END_DESC

